### Skills API Documentation
### Complete API documentation for skills management endpoints
### All operations for creating, reading, updating, and deleting skills

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@contentType = application/json
@token = your-jwt-token-here
@skillId = your-skill-uuid-here
@specificationId = your-specification-uuid-here

### ============================================
### VARIABLES SETUP
### ============================================
### Replace the variables above with actual values:
### - @token: JWT token from /api/auth/verify-otp (if authentication is required)
### - @skillId: UUID of an existing skill
### - @specificationId: UUID of an existing specification (optional)

### ============================================
### 1. CREATE SKILL
### ============================================
### Create a new skill
### Public endpoint (authentication may be required based on your setup)
### specificationId is optional - skills can exist without being linked to a specification

POST {{baseUrl}}/skills
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "JavaScript",
  "specificationId": null
}

### Example: Create Skill with Specification
POST {{baseUrl}}/skills
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "React",
  "specificationId": "{{specificationId}}"
}

### Example: Create Skill without Specification
POST {{baseUrl}}/skills
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Node.js"
}

### Response Example (201 Created):
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Skill created successfully",
###   "data": {
###     "id": "skill-uuid",
###     "name": "JavaScript",
###     "specificationId": null,
###     "createdAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z",
###     "updatedAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z"
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### 2. GET ALL SKILLS
### ============================================
### Get all skills with pagination and optional search
### Public endpoint (no authentication required)
### Query Parameters:
###   - page: Page number (default: 1)
###   - limit: Items per page (default: 100, max: 500)
###   - search: Search term to filter skills by name (optional)

### Get All Skills (Default - First Page, 100 items)
GET {{baseUrl}}/skills
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Get All Skills with Pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/skills?page=1&limit=10
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Get All Skills with Search
GET {{baseUrl}}/skills?page=1&limit=10&search=javascript
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Get All Skills - Second Page
GET {{baseUrl}}/skills?page=2&limit=20
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Response Example:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Skills fetched successfully",
###   "data": [
###     {
###       "id": "skill-uuid",
###       "name": "JavaScript",
###       "specificationId": "spec-uuid",
###       "createdAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z",
###       "updatedAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z"
###     }
###   ],
###   "pagination": {
###     "page": 1,
###     "limit": 10,
###     "totalPages": 5,
###     "totalItems": 50,
###     "hasNextPage": true,
###     "hasPreviousPage": false
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### 3. GET SKILL BY ID
### ============================================
### Get a specific skill by its ID
### Public endpoint (no authentication required)

GET {{baseUrl}}/skills/{{skillId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Response Example:
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Skill fetched successfully",
###   "data": {
###     "id": "skill-uuid",
###     "name": "JavaScript",
###     "specificationId": "spec-uuid",
###     "createdAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z",
###     "updatedAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z"
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### 4. UPDATE SKILL
### ============================================
### Update an existing skill
### Public endpoint (authentication may be required based on your setup)
### At least one field must be provided for update

PUT {{baseUrl}}/skills/{{skillId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "JavaScript ES6+"
}

### Example: Update Skill Name and Specification
PUT {{baseUrl}}/skills/{{skillId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "React.js",
  "specificationId": "{{specificationId}}"
}

### Example: Remove Specification Link
PUT {{baseUrl}}/skills/{{skillId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "specificationId": null
}

### Response Example (200 OK):
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Skill updated successfully",
###   "data": {
###     "id": "skill-uuid",
###     "name": "JavaScript ES6+",
###     "specificationId": "spec-uuid",
###     "createdAt": "2026-02-12T01:00:00.000Z",
###     "updatedAt": "2026-02-12T02:00:00.000Z"
###   }
### }

### ============================================
### 5. DELETE SKILL
### ============================================
### Delete a skill by ID
### Public endpoint (authentication may be required based on your setup)

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/skills/{{skillId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Response Example (200 OK):
### {
###   "success": true,
###   "message": "Skill deleted successfully"
### }

### ============================================
### COMPREHENSIVE NOTES & GUIDELINES
### ============================================

### 1. AUTHENTICATION & AUTHORIZATION
###    - Check your route configuration to see if authentication is required
###    - If authentication is required, use: Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
###    - Get token from: POST /api/auth/verify-otp

### 2. VALIDATION RULES
###    Create Skill:
###    - name: Required, string, 1-100 characters
###    - specificationId: Optional, must be valid UUID or null
###    
###    Update Skill:
###    - At least one field must be provided
###    - name: Optional, string, 1-100 characters if provided
###    - specificationId: Optional, must be valid UUID or null if provided

### 3. PAGINATION
###    - Default page: 1
###    - Default limit: 100
###    - Maximum limit: 500
###    - Search is case-insensitive and searches skill names

### 4. ERROR RESPONSES
###    
###    Validation Error (400):
###    {
###      "success": false,
###      "message": "Validation error message",
###      "errors": [
###        {
###          "field": "name",
###          "message": "Skill name must be at least 1 character long"
###        }
###      ]
###    }
###    
###    Not Found (404):
###    {
###      "success": false,
###      "message": "Skill not found"
###    }

### 5. SUCCESS RESPONSES
###    
###    Create Skill (201):
###    {
###      "success": true,
###      "message": "Skill created successfully",
###      "data": { ... }
###    }
###    
###    Get Skills (200):
###    {
###      "success": true,
###      "message": "Skills fetched successfully",
###      "data": [ ... ],
###      "pagination": { ... }
###    }
###    
###    Update Skill (200):
###    {
###      "success": true,
###      "message": "Skill updated successfully",
###      "data": { ... }
###    }
###    
###    Delete Skill (200):
###    {
###      "success": true,
###      "message": "Skill deleted successfully"
###    }

### 6. BEST PRACTICES
###    - Use descriptive skill names
###    - Link skills to specifications when appropriate
###    - Use search functionality to find existing skills before creating duplicates
###    - Update skills rather than creating duplicates
###    - Delete unused skills to keep the database clean

### 7. COMMON USE CASES
###    
###    Case 1: Create a new skill
###    1. POST /api/skills with name and optional specificationId
###    2. Skill is created and returned
###    
###    Case 2: Search for skills
###    1. GET /api/skills?search=javascript
###    2. Returns matching skills with pagination
###    
###    Case 3: Link skill to specification
###    1. PUT /api/skills/:id with specificationId
###    2. Skill is updated with specification link
###    
###    Case 4: Remove specification link
###    1. PUT /api/skills/:id with specificationId: null
###    2. Skill is updated to remove specification link

### ============================================
### TESTING EXAMPLES
### ============================================

### Test: Create Skill with Long Name
POST {{baseUrl}}/skills
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Full Stack Web Development with React and Node.js",
  "specificationId": null
}

### Test: Search Skills
GET {{baseUrl}}/skills?search=react&page=1&limit=5
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

### Test: Update Only Name
PUT {{baseUrl}}/skills/{{skillId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Updated Skill Name"
}

### Test: Update Only Specification
PUT {{baseUrl}}/skills/{{skillId}}
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "specificationId": "{{specificationId}}"
}
